035 - With Songs and Honors
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 35
Topic: Worship - 

Verse 1:
[F#m]With songs [D/A]and [G]honors sounding [D/A]loud,
[A]Address the Lord [G#m]on high;
[D/A]Over [F#m]the [G]heavens [Em]He spreads [F#m]His [A]cloud,
[A]And [D/A]waters [Em/B]veil the [D/F#]sky.

Verse 2:
[F#m]He sends [D/A]His [G]showers of blessing [A]down
[A]To [D]cheer [A]the plains [G#m]below;
[D/A]He [G]makes the [A/E]grass [Em]the mountains [A]crown,
[A]And [D/A]corning [Em/B]valleys [D/F#]grow.

Verse 3:
[F#m]His steady [G]counsels change the [D/A]face
[A]Of [D]the [A]declining [G#m]year;
[D/A]He [G]bids [F#m]the [G]sun [A/E]cut [Em]short his [F#m]race,
[A]And [D/A]wintry [Em/B]days appear.

Verse 4:
[F#m]He sends [D/A]His [G]word, [F#m]and [G]melts the [D/A]snow;
[A]The [D]fields [A]no longer [G#m]mourn;
[D/A]He [G]calls [F#m]the [G]warmer [Em]gales [F#m]to [A]blow,
[A]And [D/A]bids [Bm]the [Em/B]spring return.

Verse 5:
[F#m]The changing [G]wind, the flying [D/A]cloud,
[A]Obey His mighty [G#m]word:
[D/A]With [G]songs [F#m]and [G]honors [Em]sounding [F#m]loud
[A]Praise ye [D/A]the [Bm]sovereign [D/F#]Lord!
